Z||000000||ChadMan||02-25-2000||01:16 PM||||It's 70 degrees and sunny today, so instead of going to the company potluck, an attractive female coworker and I (just friends) decided to duck out and eat lunch in the park.<P>"Why don't you drive," she says.  "Your car is just so much cooler and more summery than mine."<P>POP!  Out comes the sunroof, down go the windows.  A quick stop by Mickey D's and we're heading up Riverside Drive.  The sun's beating down, geese are flying by over the river, and the Duke is blatting happily away.<P>As the boys in the beer commercial say, "It doesn't get any better than this."||||reg||6
Z||000001||bHooper||02-25-2000||02:00 PM||||Yes it is a beautifull fiero day!  It's 77 degrees, here in sunny Greenboro, North Carolina!  <P>Unfortunately, it is 45 and overcast where my GT is... the garage, on jackstands  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Although, I am proud to say that I have spent my lunch time looking for a tranny or another car... and may have found both!<P>Sorry to digress  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>For those of you fortunate to enjoy today and this weekend in you fiero's... I HATE YOU!  JK  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Have fun!!!!<P>Signed,<BR>stuck with his Jeep||||reg||1
Z||000002||Motorhead||02-25-2000||02:53 PM||||You're not alone, spent the day in Marion,SC, at my girlfriends. Leaving for my place near Myrtle Beach in a few.  Unfortunately driving her Accord.  Mine is on jackstands at the house awaiting parts.  Take heart though, spring is coming! ||||reg||6
